  - language shift
  - substrate continuity
  - historical linguistics
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  Clean public replication package for the JLG submission. Extends a
  prior demographic-modeling submission (currently under review) with
  a coordinate-anchored 18x32 Balkan grid, seven-region polygon
  classification, proportional fortification anchoring, per-region
  outputs, three substrate placement configurations (none / uniform /
  cbi_only), a 144-cell parameter sweep across substrate fractions and
  reverse-assimilation rates, paper-ready canonical tables, and five
  publication-quality geographic map figures. The headline empirical
  finding is that the cbi_only configuration at engine default
  parameters (substrate_fraction = 0.30, reverse_assimilation_rate
  = 0.030 for slavic1, fortification_anchor_fraction = 0.30)
  qualitatively reproduces the observed Slavic-toponym regional gradient
  (high Carpatho-Balkan Interior, low coastal destinations).
